{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"seagoing-illsorted-maltesedog","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# The issuelinks snapshot-enrichment merge is inline, so its guard test hand-mirrors it and will drift\n\n## The problem\n\n`fetcher.py:592-596` merges `client.get_issuelinks_map()` into the snapshot inline inside\n`fetch_snapshot`. There is no named, directly-callable helper, so a unit test cannot exercise the real\nmerge without standing up a whole fetcher.\n\nChange 1276 (bug `2b16-9be0-a8f5-41d9`) therefore had to reproduce it as `_enrich_like_fetcher`, a\nbyte-faithful HAND COPY that quotes the original. Its implementing agent flagged this itself as the\nweakest link in the change, and it is right to be worried:\n\n**What that copy guards is not cosmetic.** 2b16's guard **G1** decides whether an inbound link REMOVAL\nmay fire, by distinguishing \"the peer was queried and has no links\" (`\"issuelinks\"` key PRESENT, possibly\nan empty list) from \"we never observed this issue's links\" (key ABSENT — enrichment failed, HTTP 410, a\nfail-open partial map, or the issue fell outside a truncated page). If the production merge ever changes\nso that key-presence stops meaning \"observed\", **G1 silently stops protecting and the removal path starts\ndeleting local deps from truncated reads** — while the hand copy keeps the test green.\n\nThis epic has already fixed THREE silent-truncation defects in this exact data path (change 1105;\n`9263-b404-cb6c-463f`; `deac-4f5a-856a-49bd`, measured losing 92% of a snapshot). Turning those READ\nbugs into a WRITE bug is the worst outcome available here, and a drifting test copy is precisely how it\nwould happen without anyone noticing.\n\n## Note on scope\n\nBug `88d9-fe42-e50f-4067` carries an acceptance criterion to extract the sibling **parent** enrichment\nmerge for the same reason, so the pattern will already exist when this is picked up — this ticket is the\n**issuelinks** half. Do them the same way.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] the issuelinks enrichment merge is a named, directly-callable helper, and `fetch_snapshot` calls it\n      rather than inlining it — behaviour-preserving, pinned by a characterization assertion taken BEFORE\n      the extraction\n- [ ] 2b16's `_enrich_like_fetcher` hand copy is DELETED and its test drives the real helper\n- [ ] a test asserts the property G1 depends on: an issue observed with zero links yields the\n      `\"issuelinks\"` key PRESENT (empty list), and an issue the map never mentioned yields the key ABSENT\n- [ ] mutation-checked: changing the merge so an unobserved issue gains an empty `issuelinks` list must\n      turn a test RED, because that is the exact drift that would disarm G1","id":"6c0a-65b6-55a1-452a","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Extract the issuelinks snapshot-enrichment merge so 2b16's G1 guard test stops hand-mirroring it"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785728730629881001,"uuid":"263a56cc-e4f1-4338-9e6c-74fbc37945e3"}